ontology_mapping:
  ontology_id: CHEBI:752954
  ontology_label: ox bile
  ontology_source: CHEBI
  mapping_quality: NARROW_MATCH
  evidence:
  - evidence_type: LLM_SUGGESTION
    source: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/api/ontologies/chebi/terms?obo_id=CHEBI:752954
    notes: Generic ox bile is a verified broader material parent; the local ingredient
      identity preserves the explicitly desiccated preparation rather than identifying
      it with every fresh/dried bile material.
  - evidence_type: LLM_SUGGESTION
    source: https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/US/en/product/sial/70168
    notes: The source ingredient is desiccated ox bile, a dried bovine bile material.
      NBRC1004 and NBRC1390 independently name desiccated ox bile as a weighed dry
      ingredient; Sigma70168 confirms the material is produced by dehydrating fresh
      ox bile. This is neither fresh liquid bile nor an isolated bile salt, and no
      supplier-specific grade or constituent concentration is asserted. Generic ox-bile
      owners and Oxgall are recorded reconciliation candidates, not automatically
      merged or equated to this explicitly dried material.
